<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23304" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακρύω</span></b> , first in <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Ch.</u>
			81
		</span></i>: fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					658
				</span></i>
			, later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					404
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδάκρῡσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.112
				</span></i>
			, etc., 
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρῡσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.55
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδάκρῡκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					2.3.14
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακρύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					815
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακρύσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					431
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, pres., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1226
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδάκρῡμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.7
				</span></i>
			, etc.: [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υ</span> long in all tenses,
			except in late Poets, as <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.148
			</span></i>]: (for the Root, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυ</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> intr.,
				<i>weep, shed tears,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.: c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ.
			γόους</span> to lament <i>with tears,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				580
			</span></i>: c. gen. causae, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. συμφορᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					528
				</span></i>
			 (dub. l.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. βλέφαρα</span>
			<i>to flood</i> them <i>with tears,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				948
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. χαρᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					7.2.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ταῖς συμφοραῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					4.168
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδάκρυμαι</span>
			<i>to be in tears,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίπτε δεδάκρυσαι, Πατρόκλεες;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδάκρυνται δὲ παρειαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.491
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδακρυμένος</span>”
				<i>in tears,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					364b
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Publ.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the
			eyes, <i>run,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				620a5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of trees,
				<i>exude gum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				121
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλεκτρον δακρύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Salt.</u>
					55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>weep for,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1490
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1486
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1027
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be wept for,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμφορὰ δακρύεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1226
				</span></i>
			 (prob. 
				Med.
			 in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				815
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
